  <prompt>Compose the single shared React 19 `EmailWorkspace` component in `@spaarke/communication-components` — the ONE component both mounts render. It wires the left `EmailCardList` (030) + `ViewSelector` (031) into the reading-pane shell (032) which composes the `.eml` render branch (033), envelope header + attachments (034), associations review + tracking (035), and compose/toolbar (036). This single source of truth guarantees dual-mount parity (NFR-06): one bug fix propagates to both the SpaarkeAi widget (041) and the standalone code page (042). Follow the dual-use Pattern D reference `CommunicationsWorkspaceWidget.tsx` / `CalendarWorkspaceWidget.tsx`. Do NOT author mount-specific logic here — mounts are thin wrappers over this component.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in React 19 + Fluent UI v9 shared-lib composition and the SpaarkeAi dual-use Pattern D. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A single exported `EmailWorkspace` React 19 component in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/` (barrel-exported from `@spaarke/communication-components`) that renders the full Outlook-style two-pane Email surface by composing the Phase-3 sub-views, and is consumed IDENTICALLY by both the widget mount (041) and the code-page mount (042). The component owns all surface state (selected card, active view, loading/empty/error states) and takes only host-agnostic props (e.g. an `IDataverseClient`/data adapter + `authenticatedFetch`) — no PCF context, no mount-specific branching.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-01 + NFR-06 + Success Criterion 1: the Email surface must open as BOTH a SpaarkeAi workspace widget and a standalone code page, rendering identically, from ONE shared component. Design Lens 2 fixes this as dual-use Pattern D ("Both mount the same React 19 shared-lib component — single source of truth"). Phases 0–3 built the pieces: `sanitizeEmailHtml` (001), the `.eml` render branch (033), `EmailCardList` (030), `ViewSelector` integration (031), the reading-pane shell (032), header/attachments (034), associations/tracking (035), and compose/toolbar (036). This task assembles them; 041/042 are thin mounts over the result.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/EmailWorkspace.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/index.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/widgets/CommunicationsWorkspaceWidget/CommunicationsWorkspaceWidget.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Events.Components/src/widgets/CalendarWorkspaceWidget/CalendarWorkspaceWidget.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/communications.registration.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="033" status="pending">`.eml` render branch (sandboxed iframe + `sprk_body` degradation).</dependency>
      <dependency task="034" status="pending">Envelope header (`CommunicationHeader`) + attachments view.</dependency>
      <dependency task="035" status="pending">Associations review (interactive/additive) + tracking view.</dependency>
      <dependency task="036" status="pending">Compose reuse (Reply/ReplyAll/Fwd/New) + "Open full form" modal.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Dual-mount parity (NFR-06): `EmailWorkspace` is the SINGLE source of truth for the surface. It MUST NOT contain any mount-specific branching (no `if (isWidget)` / `if (isCodePage)`); mounts 041/042 wrap it thinly. Any surface behavior lives here so one fix propagates to both.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">This component and every sub-view it composes are React 19 (code page / widget layer). It MUST NOT be shared into any PCF and MUST NOT introduce an `as React.ComponentType` cast on this new code-page work (NFR-05, slim-first). PCFs keep their React 16/17 views.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 only; theme (light/dark) is inherited from the host `FluentProvider` — this component MUST NOT mount its own `FluentProvider` (the mounts own theming). Renders correctly in dark mode.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">All BFF calls (`.eml` render) go through `@spaarke/auth` `authenticatedFetch` supplied by the host — no new auth surface, no token snapshots.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse only: compose the existing sub-views (033–036) + `EmailCardList`/`ViewSelector`/`PanelSplitter`. MUST NOT fork a composer (canonical `EmailComposer`/`SendEmailDialog` via 036) and MUST NOT re-implement association/attachment/tracking logic (consume the Layer-1 cores from 020–023).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>SpaarkeAi dual-use Pattern D + shared-lib composition</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-component-library.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-v9-adoption.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKEAI-DASHBOARD-AND-WIDGET-MODEL.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Pattern D dual-use widget" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/widgets/CommunicationsWorkspaceWidget/CommunicationsWorkspaceWidget.tsx">The reference rich Pattern D widget — host-agnostic props, self-contained state, no `FluentProvider`. Mirror its shape for `EmailWorkspace`.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Barrel export" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/index.ts">Export `EmailWorkspace` (and its props type) so both mounts import from `@spaarke/communication-components`.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load this project's CLAUDE.md + spec FR-01/NFR-06 + design Lens 2. Declare RIGOR LEVEL: FULL with reason. Confirm 033–036 are ✅ before composing.</step>
    <step order="1">Define `EmailWorkspaceProps` — host-agnostic: a Dataverse data adapter (`IDataverseClient` / `Xrm.WebApi` shim), an `authenticatedFetch` for the `.eml` render call, and optional initial view id. No PCF context type.</step>
    <step order="2">Author `EmailWorkspace.tsx`: `PanelSplitter` two-pane layout — left = `ViewSelector` (031) over `sprk_communication` Email saved views + `EmailCardList` (030); right = the reading-pane shell (032) hosting header/attachments (034), `.eml` body branch (033), associations/tracking (035), and the full-width toolbar/compose (036).</step>
    <step order="3">Own surface state centrally: selected card id, active saved view, and the loading/empty/error/uncertainty states (spec FR-19) — header paints from the loaded record while the `.eml` body swaps in when the render returns.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify NO mount-specific branching and NO self-mounted `FluentProvider`; theme flows from the host. Confirm no `as React.ComponentType` cast (NFR-05).</step>
    <step order="5">Barrel-export `EmailWorkspace` + `EmailWorkspaceProps` from `src/index.ts`.</step>
    <step order="6">Build the shared lib (`npm run build` — NOT a PCF build) and run its unit tests; add/adjust a smoke render test that mounts `EmailWorkspace` under a `FluentProvider` (test host) in both `webLightTheme` and `webDarkTheme`.</step>
    <step order="7">Update `projects/email-communication-solution-r5/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 040 to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document the `EmailWorkspaceProps` contract (what each mount must supply) in `projects/email-communication-solution-r5/notes/` for 041/042.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If dual-mount parity cannot be achieved without mount-specific branching inside `EmailWorkspace` (e.g. the widget host and code-page host require structurally different data access that cannot be abstracted behind one adapter prop), STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 rather than forking behavior into two code paths.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`CommunicationsWorkspaceWidget.tsx` (rich Pattern D chat/thread widget) and `CommunicationPage` (single-record page) — the closest neighbors in `@spaarke/communication-components`.</existing>
    <extension>No — `CommunicationsWorkspaceWidget` is the multi-channel chat/thread metaphor and `CommunicationPage` is single-record; the Outlook mail master/detail surface (flat card list + reading-pane "as sent") is a distinct metaphor and entry point. It reuses the same lib + Pattern D pipeline (not forked).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without one shared `EmailWorkspace`, the widget and code page would each assemble the sub-views independently, so a reading-pane bug fixed in one mount silently persists in the other — the exact dual-mount-drift failure NFR-06/Success Criterion 1 exist to prevent, and there is no standalone mailbox destination.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Dual-mount parity smoke">
      <steps><step>Render `EmailWorkspace` with a stub data adapter (one Email record with quoted `.eml`).</step><step>Select the card.</step></steps>
      <expected>Left card list + right reading pane render; header paints from the record, `.eml` body swaps in — identical DOM regardless of host wrapper.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Render `EmailWorkspace` under `FluentProvider theme={webDarkTheme}`.</step></steps>
      <expected>Two-pane surface + toolbar render legibly in dark mode; no hardcoded light colors; contrast preserved.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools><tool name="npm">Build/test the shared lib (`npm run build`, NOT a PCF build)</tool><tool name="terminal">shell</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/EmailWorkspace.tsx</output>
