  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the built `@spaarke/communication-components`, when `EmailWorkspace` is imported and rendered with a data adapter, then it renders the two-pane surface composing `EmailCardList` + `ViewSelector` + reading-pane shell + all Phase-3 sub-views (033–036).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same `EmailWorkspace` component, when rendered by two different host wrappers (widget-style and code-page-style), then the produced surface is identical (dual-mount parity) — verified by the parity smoke test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a selected Email card with a `.eml` archive, when the card is clicked, then the header paints from the record and the `.eml` body swaps into the reading pane (loading→loaded state transition).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `EmailWorkspace` contains NO mount-specific branch (`isWidget`/`isCodePage`) and mounts no `FluentProvider` of its own — theme is inherited from the host (grep + review).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (NFR-05): no `as React.ComponentType` cast is introduced on this component; it imports no PCF `ComponentFramework` type.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`EmailWorkspace` renders legibly under `webDarkTheme` (ADR-021 dark-mode ui-test passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All shared-lib unit tests pass; the lib build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference spec FR-01 + NFR-06 + Success Criterion 1; design Lens 2 (target surfaces, Pattern D). This is `parallel-safe:false` — the composition root 041/042 consume. Run `/conflict-check` before opening the PR (shared `@spaarke/communication-components`).

  COMPLETED 2026-07-28. Full details: `projects/email-communication-solution-r5/notes/task-040-email-workspace-assembly.md`. Summary: built `EmailWorkspace` composition root under `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/EmailWorkspace/**` (types + mapping helpers + `useEmailWorkspaceRecord` hook + the component + barrel + 7 tests), wiring `EmailViewSelector`/`EmailCardList` (030/031) into `EmailReadingPaneShell` (032) with all 5 render slots filled by the Phase-3 sub-views (033/034/035) and `useEmailComposeActions`/`OpenFullFormButton` (036). Appended one barrel line to `src/components/index.ts`. All acceptance criteria verified (incl. the `.eml`-archive-present path via a dedicated test). Build/lint/tests all green (14/14 suites, 97/97 tests package-wide). Quality gates (code-review + adr-check) run: 0 Critical/Violations. One test-infra fix required (documented as Deviation 1 in the notes file): extended `jest.config.cjs`'s existing React/ReactDOM dedup pattern to also dedupe `@fluentui/react-components`/`@fluentui/react-tabster`/`tabster`, root-causing a cross-package Fluent version-mismatch crash discovered while testing the composition (not a defect in any consumed sub-view). One flagged-not-invented gap carried forward: the three tracking fields (`monitor`/`highPriority`/`accessPermission`) use placeholder Dataverse logical names pending schema creation (design.md already flags this form placement as "net-new") — file via `/defer` before task 090.</notes>

